# Refactor Plan: Restore Missing Methods in cli_engine.py

## Problem
After refactoring cli.py to be modular, the list and show commands stopped working because certain methods are missing from tasks_ai/cli_engine.py that are being called by the command modules.

## Root Cause
During the modularization process, some methods were not properly transferred from the monolithic cli.py to the new cli_engine.py module. Specifically:
- Methods called by command modules (like list, show, etc.) are missing from cli_engine.py
- The TasksCLI class in cli_engine.py needs to have these methods restored

## Solution Approach
1. Identify which methods are being called by command modules on the cli object
2. Compare with what methods currently exist in cli_engine.py
3. Copy the missing method implementations from the original monolithic cli.py.main
4. Add them to cli_engine.py in the appropriate locations

